---
import CaseStudyLayout from '../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const email = site.email || 'janehoudesign@gmail.com';

const nav = [
  { label: 'Context', href: '#context' },
  { label: 'Outcome', href: '#outcome' },
  { label: 'Takeaways', href: '#takeaways' },
  { label: 'Insights', href: '#insights' },
];
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="Migration Dashboard"
  heading="Leading design of 0 → 1 internal tooling"
  role="Product Designer"
  team="1 Product Manager, 3 Developers"
  timeline="March 2026 – August 2026"
  projectType="Product Design"
  nav={nav}
  commentId="case-study-migration"
>
  <section id="context" data-comment-id="migration-context">
    <h3>Context</h3>
    <p class="lead">
      An internal platform shipped in beta to help developers and technical program managers (TPMs)
      manage and run mass code migrations. I joined as the sole designer, defining design direction
      and what success looked like.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="outcome" data-comment-id="migration-outcome">
    <h3>Outcome</h3>
    <p class="lead">
      I led 10 user tests with TPMs and engineers and delivered 6 core features for
      implementation. Early estimates suggest the migration workflows could save about a day per
      customer project, supporting AI-accelerated workflows and design-system adoption.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="takeaways" data-comment-id="migration-takeaways">
    <h3>Takeaways</h3>
    <p class="lead">
      I learned how to navigate ambiguity in an early-stage product and establish design’s position
      on the project with the team. I led user research when there weren’t dedicated researchers, and
      vibe-coded design iterations in code branching from production to closely replicate the
      end-user experience. Though I didn’t get to see the long-tail impact and continue iterating on
      my designs, I laid the groundwork for future iteration and advocated for web analytics tracking
      so the team could gather a clearer baseline going forward.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="insights" data-comment-id="migration-insights" class="migration-insights">
    <h3>Insights / quotes</h3>
    <div class="migration-quotes">
      <figure class="migration-quote">
        <blockquote>
          <p>
            I can't thank you enough, Jane! You really stepped up when the team needed you. I am so
            glad that I could rely on you. I have been stretched thin with a lot of ongoing work on
            product, program and engineering side so I had to shift my focus and priorities and you
            were there to help fill in and bring customer perspective/needs to the team… Your impact
            was so high and valuable that it feels like you've been on the team for a long time and
            not just a few months.
          </p>
        </blockquote>
        <figcaption>PM</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="migration-quote">
        <blockquote>
          <p>
            Thank you for helping to solve one of the largest, painful, and underappreciated aspects
            of our work.
          </p>
          <p>
            Great infrastructure is easy to overlook precisely because it works, and this product has
            become one of those things that quietly makes everyone else's job easier. Jane took on the
            unglamorous parts — the design decisions, the edge cases, the maintenance that never shows
            up in a demo — and delivered something dependable enough that the rest of us get to build
            on top of it without thinking twice. Thank you for the care and craft you put into work
            that so many of us use every day.
          </p>
        </blockquote>
        <figcaption>Prospective user</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="migration-quote">
        <blockquote>
          <p>
            Your dedication to the product throughout your internship has been outstanding. You
            consistently went above and beyond—diving deep into user needs, iterating quickly on
            feedback, and delivering design work that made a real, measurable difference to the
            product experience. Thank you for your hard work, creativity, and commitment.
          </p>
        </blockquote>
        <figcaption>Developer on the team</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="migration-quote">
        <blockquote>
          <p>
            Thanks a bunch. That was clearly a very productive collaboration & I appreciate the way
            you took around designing the interface & thinking of user stories.
          </p>
          <p>
            I really appreciate that you dive deep into understanding how the user operates, what's of
            value to them. This drives the product forward exactly where users expect us to.
          </p>
        </blockquote>
        <figcaption>Developer on the project</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section data-comment-id="migration-nda">
    <aside class="migration-disclaimer" role="note" aria-label="NDA notice">
      <p>
        I’m not able to publicize this work due to an NDA. If you’d like to learn more, please
        <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>contact me personally</a> for details.
      </p>
    </aside>
  </section>
</CaseStudyLayout>

<style>
  .migration-quotes {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .migration-quote {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 1.15rem 1.25rem;
    background: #f7f7f7;
    border: none;
  }

  .migration-quote blockquote {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border: none;
  }

  .migration-quote blockquote p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-ink);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .migration-quote blockquote p + p {
    margin-top: 0.875rem;
  }

  .migration-quote blockquote p:first-child::before {
    content: '“';
  }

  .migration-quote blockquote p:last-child::after {
    content: '”';
  }

  .migration-quote figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .migration-disclaimer {
    padding: 1rem 0;
    background: transparent;
  }

  .migration-disclaimer p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .migration-disclaimer a {
    color: var(--color-ink);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 0.15em;
    transition: opacity 0.15s ease;
  }

  .migration-disclaimer a:hover {
    opacity: 0.7;
  }
</style>
